-- Q10076: Public Company Reporting [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 260-10-45-10, shares are included in the weighted-average from their issuance date. Weighted-average shares = (200,000 x 6/12) + (240,000 x 6/12) = 220,000. Basic EPS = $660,000 / 220,000 = $3.00.
Wrong (B): $2.75 incorrectly uses 240,000 shares for the full year ($660,000 / 240,000), ignoring the weighting requirement.
Wrong (C): $3.30 uses only the beginning 200,000 shares ($660,000 / 200,000), ignoring the mid-year issuance entirely.
Wrong (D): $3.67 divides net income by a weighted-average that underweights the new shares, producing an inflated EPS figure.$EXPL$
