Wrong (A): $15,000 represents the pre-tax half-year interest ($500,000 x 6% x 6/12) without applying the 25% tax adjustment required by the if-converted method.
Wrong (B): $22,500 represents the full-year after-tax interest ($500,000 x 6% x 0.75), incorrectly treating the bonds as if they were outstanding for 12 months.
Wrong (D): $30,000 represents the full-year pre-tax interest ($500,000 x 6%), ignoring both the mid-year conversion and the tax effect.$EXPL$
