Wrong (A): The stock options add only 7,500 incremental shares with no numerator adjustment, producing a smaller absolute improvement than the bonds'' 60,000 shares.
Wrong (B): The two strategies do not produce the same improvement because the securities differ in per-share impact, incremental shares, and numerator effects.
