-- Q10458: Public Company Reporting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 260-10-45-22, stock options are included in diluted EPS from the grant date. The 15,000 options at $30 exercise price produce 6,000 incremental shares (15,000 - $450,000/$50), but weighted for only six months (July through December), only 3,000 shares are added to the denominator.
Wrong (A): While the treasury stock method uses the period''s average price, the resulting incremental shares must still be weighted for the portion of the year the options were outstanding.
Wrong (B): Mid-year grants do not produce higher incremental shares; the same treasury stock calculation applies, but the result is then time-weighted to a lower figure.
Wrong (D): Options are not excluded simply because they were granted mid-year; ASC 260 includes them from the grant date with appropriate time-weighting.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10458;

-- Q10546: Public Company Reporting [hard/L3]
