Wrong (B): The adjustment factor increases prior-year shares (multiplying by a factor above 1.0), which decreases restated EPS rather than increasing it.
Wrong (C): A below-market subscription price creates a bonus element requiring retroactive adjustment, unlike a simple issuance at market value.
