  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 87, paragraphs 52-53, a government lessor recognizes a lease receivable at the present value of lease payments ($463,000) and a corresponding deferred inflow of resources. The deferred inflow is amortized as lease revenue systematically over the 8-year lease term. The underlying capital asset is not derecognized.
Wrong (A): The building''s carrying value is not removed from capital assets; the lessor retains ownership and continues reporting the capital asset.
Wrong (C): No capital asset derecognition occurs under GASB 87 lessor accounting, and unearned revenue is not the proper classification for the offset.
