-- Q11374: State and Local Government [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, paragraphs 86-87, governmental funds use the current financial resources measurement focus. Bond proceeds are classified as other financing sources because they create an obligation rather than an inflow from operations or nonexchange transactions.
Wrong (A): Bond proceeds are not revenue because they represent borrowed funds that must be repaid, not earned resources.
Wrong (C): Governmental funds do not report long-term liabilities on their balance sheets; the bond liability appears only in government-wide statements.
Wrong (D): Deferred inflows of resources relate to revenue recognition timing, not to debt proceeds received for capital projects.$EXPL$
