-- Q11376: State and Local Government [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB 54 and GASB 34 budgetary guidance, lapsing encumbrances are reversed at fiscal year-end because the related appropriations expire. When equipment is delivered in the new year, the $148,000 is charged as an expenditure against new fiscal year appropriations.
Wrong (A): Encumbrances are budgetary accounts that reserve fund balance, not liabilities. Lapsing encumbrances do not carry forward on the balance sheet.
Wrong (B): Lapsing encumbrances do not carry forward as committed fund balance, and expenditures in the new year are charged to new-year appropriations, not prior-year ones.
Wrong (D): Encumbrances do not convert to accounts payable; they are reversed, and the actual payable is recorded only when goods are received and invoiced.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11376;

