-- Q11381: State and Local Government [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB 62, paragraphs 78-80, a change in useful life is a change in accounting estimate applied prospectively. After 7 years, accumulated depreciation is $1,960,000 ($8,400,000 / 30 x 7), leaving $6,440,000. Dividing by the new remaining life of 28 years yields $230,000.
Wrong (A): $280,000 continues the original schedule ($8,400,000 / 30), ignoring the engineering study''s revised estimate entirely.
Wrong (B): $240,000 divides the original cost by a new total life of 35 years, which improperly applies the change retroactively instead of prospectively.
