-- Q11383: State and Local Government [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB 33, paragraph 20, voluntary nonexchange transactions with time requirements are recognized as revenue in the period specified. Because funds may not be spent before January 1, 2028, the $2,000,000 received in 2026 is reported as a deferred inflow of resources until the time requirement is met.
Wrong (B): The time requirement is an eligibility condition that delays revenue recognition even though cash was received; receipt alone does not satisfy eligibility.
Wrong (C): Revenue cannot be recognized while the time requirement remains unsatisfied. Restricting net position does not substitute for deferred inflow treatment.
Wrong (D): The pledge is a voluntary nonexchange transaction, not a liability. The city does not owe the funds back to the foundation.$EXPL$
