  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB 34, paragraph 67, enterprise fund reporting is mandatory only when: (1) debt is secured solely by pledged fees, (2) laws require cost recovery through fees, or (3) pricing policies are designed to recover costs. The golf course fails all three criteria since debt is backed by general revenues and fees cover only 45%.
Wrong (A): Merely charging fees to external users does not trigger mandatory enterprise fund reporting; all three GASB 34 criteria must be evaluated.
